<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1.0">
<meta name="description" content="Raju Driving School learning hub — structured basic driving lessons based on the IDTR Basic Driving Lessons syllabus.">
<title>Learn the Road | Raju Driving School</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700;800&family=Manrope:wght@700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="./styles.css">
<style>
.learn-page{background:#f7f9fc;color:var(--ink)}
.learn-nav{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:60;width:100%;height:78px;padding:0 clamp(20px,5vw,72px);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;background:rgba(255,255,255,.84);backdrop-filter:blur(20px);border-bottom:1px solid rgba(219,228,239,.9)}
.learn-nav .brand-logo{width:78px;height:56px}.learn-nav-links{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:28px;font-size:.75rem;font-weight:800;color:#4b5d75}.learn-nav-links a:hover{color:var(--blue)}
.learn-hero{position:relative;overflow:hidden;padding:clamp(76px,9vw,135px) clamp(20px,8vw,120px) 90px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fff 0%,#f6f9fd 60%,#edf5ff 100%)}
.learn-hero:before{content:"";position:absolute;width:46vw;height:46vw;right:-18vw;top:-22vw;border-radius:50%;background:radial-gradient(circle,rgba(255,210,31,.48),rgba(255,210,31,0) 68%)}
.learn-hero-grid{position:relative;z-index:2;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.05fr .75fr;gap:8vw;align-items:center;max-width:1400px;margin:auto}
.learn-kicker{color:var(--blue);font-size:.68rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.2em}.learn-hero h1{font:800 clamp(4rem,7.6vw,8.2rem)/.86 Manrope;letter-spacing:-.065em;margin:20px 0 28px}.learn-hero h1 span{color:var(--blue)}.learn-hero h1 em{font-style:normal;color:var(--red)}
.learn-hero p{max-width:670px;color:var(--muted);font-size:1.04rem;line-height:1.8}.learn-hero-actions{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:30px}.learn-source-note{margin-top:18px;font-size:.68rem;color:#7b899b}
.learn-hero-visual{position:relative;min-height:440px}.learn-visual-card{position:absolute;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e0e8f2;border-radius:28px;box-shadow:0 25px 80px rgba(10,48,105,.13);overflow:hidden}.learn-visual-main{inset:15px 0 30px 40px}.learn-visual-main img{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover}.learn-visual-main figcaption{position:absolute;left:18px;right:18px;bottom:18px;padding:15px 17px;border-radius:17px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.9);backdrop-filter:blur(12px)}.learn-visual-main strong{display:block;font:900 .95rem Manrope}.learn-visual-main span{display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:.68rem;margin-top:4px}.learn-visual-mini{left:0;bottom:0;width:205px;padding:18px}.learn-visual-mini strong{font:900 2rem Manrope;color:var(--blue)}.learn-visual-mini span{display:block;font-size:.62rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.4;color:#607188;margin-top:4px}
.learn-overview{padding:90px clamp(20px,8vw,120px);background:#fff}.learn-overview-inner{max-width:1400px;margin:auto}.learn-overview-head{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr .62fr;gap:8vw;align-items:end}.learn-overview h2,.learn-lessons-head h2{font:800 clamp(3.3rem,6vw,6.5rem)/.9 Manrope;letter-spacing:-.06em;margin:17px 0 0}.learn-overview h2 span,.learn-lessons-head h2 span{color:var(--blue)}.learn-overview-head>p{color:var(--muted);line-height:1.8;margin:0 0 7px}.learn-stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:14px;margin-top:48px}.learn-stat{padding:24px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:22px;background:linear-gradient(145deg,#fff,#f6f9fc);box-shadow:0 15px 45px rgba(10,48,105,.055)}.learn-stat strong{display:block;font:900 2.5rem Manrope;color:var(--blue)}.learn-stat span{display:block;margin-top:5px;font-size:.7rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5d6f87}
.learn-lessons{padding:100px clamp(20px,8vw,120px);background:linear-gradient(180deg,#f7f9fc,#eef4fa)}.learn-lessons-inner{max-width:1400px;margin:auto}.learn-lessons-head{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr .6fr;gap:8vw;align-items:end}.learn-lessons-head>p{color:var(--muted);line-height:1.8;margin:0}.lesson-filter{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:35px 0 28px}.lesson-filter button{border:1px solid #d7e1ed;background:#fff;color:#51637a;border-radius:999px;padding:9px 14px;font-size:.67rem;font-weight:900;cursor:pointer}.lesson-filter button.active{background:var(--blue);border-color:var(--blue);color:#fff}
.lesson-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:17px}.lesson-card{background:#fff;border:1px solid #dce5ef;border-radius:24px;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:0 15px 45px rgba(10,48,105,.065);transition:transform .25s,box-shadow .25s}.lesson-card:hover{transform:translateY(-4px);box-shadow:0 24px 60px rgba(10,48,105,.1)}.lesson-card[hidden]{display:none}.lesson-summary{width:100%;border:0;background:none;text-align:left;padding:20px 21px;cursor:pointer;color:inherit}.lesson-top{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:12px}.lesson-number{display:grid;place-items:center;width:35px;height:35px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--blue);color:#fff;font:900 .67rem Manrope}.lesson-card:nth-child(n+13) .lesson-number{background:var(--red)}.lesson-page{font-size:.55rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#8795a8}.lesson-summary h3{font:900 1.08rem/1.15 Manrope;margin:18px 0 8px}.lesson-summary p{margin:0;color:var(--muted);font-size:.72rem;line-height:1.55}.lesson-more{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;margin-top:15px;color:var(--blue);font-size:.62rem;font-weight:900}.lesson-more b{font-size:.95rem;transition:transform .2s}.lesson-card.open .lesson-more b{transform:rotate(90deg)}.lesson-detail{display:none;padding:0 21px 21px;border-top:1px solid #e7edf4}.lesson-card.open .lesson-detail{display:block}.lesson-detail-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:15px;padding-top:17px}.lesson-detail h4{margin:0 0 7px;font-size:.62rem;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--blue)}.lesson-detail ul{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;display:grid;gap:6px}.lesson-detail li{position:relative;padding-left:14px;color:#42566f;font-size:.68rem;line-height:1.45}.lesson-detail li:before{content:"";position:absolute;left:0;top:.52em;width:5px;height:5px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--yellow)}.lesson-detail .practice{padding:12px 13px;border-radius:14px;background:#f6f9fc;color:#4c6078;font-size:.65rem;line-height:1.5}.lesson-detail .practice strong{color:var(--red)}
.learn-path{padding:100px clamp(20px,8vw,120px);background:#fff}.learn-path-inner{max-width:1400px;margin:auto}.learn-path-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:30px;align-items:end}.learn-path-head h2{font:800 clamp(3.2rem,5.8vw,6.2rem)/.9 Manrope;letter-spacing:-.06em;margin:17px 0 0}.learn-path-head h2 span{color:var(--red)}.learn-path-head p{max-width:470px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.8}.path-steps{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(5,1fr);gap:12px;margin-top:50px}.path-step{position:relative;padding:24px;border-radius:22px;background:#f6f9fc;border:1px solid #dfe7f0}.path-step:after{content:"→";position:absolute;right:-17px;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%);width:30px;height:30px;border-radius:50%;display:grid;place-items:center;background:var(--yellow);font-weight:900;z-index:2}.path-step:last-child:after{display:none}.path-step b{display:grid;place-items:center;width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--blue);color:#fff;font:900 .65rem Manrope}.path-step h3{font:900 .95rem Manrope;margin:17px 0 7px}.path-step p{font-size:.68rem;line-height:1.5;color:var(--muted);margin:0}
.learn-cta{padding:90px clamp(20px,8vw,120px);background:var(--ink);color:#fff}.learn-cta-inner{max-width:1400px;margin:auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr .65fr;gap:8vw;align-items:center}.learn-cta h2{font:800 clamp(3.5rem,6.5vw,7rem)/.9 Manrope;letter-spacing:-.06em;margin:16px 0}.learn-cta h2 span{color:var(--yellow)}.learn-cta p{color:#c9d5e3;line-height:1.8;max-width:580px}.learn-cta-card{padding:28px;border-radius:26px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.08);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.14)}.learn-cta-card strong{font:900 1.2rem Manrope}.learn-cta-card ul{list-style:none;margin:20px 0 0;padding:0;display:grid;gap:10px}.learn-cta-card li{font-size:.72rem;color:#d7e1ed}.learn-cta-card li:before{content:"✓";color:var(--yellow);font-weight:900;margin-right:9px}
@media(max-width:1000px){.learn-hero-grid,.learn-overview-head,.learn-lessons-head,.learn-cta-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr}.learn-hero-visual{min-height:390px;max-width:650px}.lesson-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.learn-stats{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.path-steps{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.path-step:after{display:none}.learn-path-head{display:block}}
@media(max-width:650px){.learn-nav{height:70px;padding:0 17px}.learn-nav-links a:not(.learn-home){display:none}.learn-nav .brand-logo{width:70px;height:52px}.learn-hero{padding:72px 20px 70px}.learn-hero h1{font-size:clamp(3.5rem,16vw,5.4rem)}.learn-hero p{font-size:.9rem}.learn-hero-visual{min-height:320px}.learn-visual-main{inset:10px 0 20px 24px}.learn-visual-mini{width:150px;padding:13px}.learn-visual-mini strong{font-size:1.7rem}.learn-overview,.learn-lessons,.learn-path,.learn-cta{padding:72px 20px}.learn-overview h2,.learn-lessons-head h2,.learn-path-head h2,.learn-cta h2{font-size:3.5rem}.learn-stats{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:10px}.learn-stat{padding:17px}.learn-stat strong{font-size:2rem}.lesson-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.lesson-summary{padding:18px}.path-steps{grid-template-columns:1fr}.learn-cta-card{padding:21px}}
</style>
</head>
<body class="learn-page">
<header class="learn-nav">
  <a class="brand" href="./index.html" aria-label="Raju Driving School home"><img class="brand-logo" src="./images/raju-logo.png" alt="Raju Driving School — Chalakudy — Since 1969"></a>
  <nav class="learn-nav-links"><a class="learn-home" href="./index.html">Home</a><a href="#lessons">Lessons</a><a href="#path">Learning path</a><a href="./mock-test.html">Mock Test</a><a href="./video-lessons.html">Video Classes</a><a class="nav-cta" href="./index.html#contact">Start Learning <span>↗</span></a></nav>
</header>
<main>
<section class="learn-hero">
  <div class="learn-hero-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="learn-kicker">LEARNING HUB · BASIC DRIVING</div>
      <h1>Know the road.<br><span>Practice the skill.</span><br><em>Drive right.</em></h1>
      <p>A practical learning hub for the fundamentals taught through our basic driving programme. Work through the lessons before, during and after your practical training — one skill at a time.</p>
      <div class="learn-hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-yellow" href="./mock-test.html">Take the mock test <b>↗</b></a><a class="btn" style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #dce5ef;color:var(--ink)" href="./index.html#courses">Back to the Raju Method</a></div>
      <div class="learn-source-note">Structured from the 29-page IDTR Basic Driving Lessons guide supplied for Raju Driving School.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="learn-hero-visual">
      <figure class="learn-visual-card learn-visual-main"><img src="./images/training-action/car-instructor-front.jpg" alt="Instructor guiding a learner during driving training"><figcaption><strong>Learn with guidance.</strong><span>Understand the principle, then practise it on the road.</span></figcaption></figure>
      <div class="learn-visual-card learn-visual-mini"><strong>25</strong><span>core lessons in the supplied basic driving syllabus</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="learn-overview">
  <div class="learn-overview-inner">
    <div class="learn-overview-head"><div><div class="learn-kicker">01 / THE COURSE MAP</div><h2>From controls to<br><span>traffic signals.</span></h2></div><p>The supplied IDTR guide progresses from getting comfortable in the cockpit to manoeuvres, junctions, parking, roundabouts and traffic signals. The lesson order below follows that progression.</p></div>
    <div class="learn-stats"><div class="learn-stat"><strong>25</strong><span>Core lessons</span></div><div class="learn-stat"><strong>01→25</strong><span>Structured sequence</span></div><div class="learn-stat"><strong>3</strong><span>Control foundations</span></div><div class="learn-stat"><strong>1</strong><span>Road-ready goal</span></div></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="learn-lessons" id="lessons">
  <div class="learn-lessons-inner">
    <div class="learn-lessons-head"><div><div class="learn-kicker">02 / BASIC DRIVING LESSONS</div><h2>Learn it <span>step by step.</span></h2></div><p>Tap any lesson to open its learning notes. The descriptions keep the terminology and progression of the supplied IDTR guide while turning the classroom material into an easier digital study format.</p></div>
    <div class="lesson-filter" role="tablist" aria-label="Filter lessons"><button class="active" data-filter="all">All 25</button><button data-filter="foundation">Foundations</button><button data-filter="road">Road skills</button><button data-filter="manoeuvres">Manoeuvres</button><button data-filter="traffic">Traffic</button></div>
    <div class="lesson-grid" id="lessonGrid">
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="foundation"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">01</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 01</span></div><h3>Cockpit Drill</h3><p>Set yourself up before the vehicle moves.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Doors, seat and steering position</li><li>Seat-belt and mirror checks</li><li>A deliberate pre-drive routine</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Start every drive from a safe, correctly adjusted position.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="foundation"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">02</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 02</span></div><h3>Foot Controls</h3><p>Understand the controls operated by your feet.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Clutch, brake and accelerator roles</li><li>Smooth, deliberate pedal operation</li><li>Coordination before moving off</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Practise each pedal separately, then combine them smoothly.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="foundation"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">03</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 03</span></div><h3>Hand Controls</h3><p>Build control of the steering and hand-operated controls.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Steering control and hand position</li><li>Indicators and other hand controls</li><li>Gear and handbrake awareness</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Use calm, precise hand movements rather than rushed inputs.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="foundation"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">04</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 04</span></div><h3>Auxiliary Controls</h3><p>Learn the controls that support safe visibility and operation.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Lighting and visibility controls</li><li>Wipers / washers and related controls</li><li>Use controls without losing road awareness</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Know where each control is before you need it on the road.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="road"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">05</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 05</span></div><h3>Signals</h3><p>Communicate your intentions clearly to other road users.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Correct and timely signalling</li><li>Signals for turning, slowing and stopping</li><li>Recognise the difference between intention and action</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Signal early enough to inform others, then complete the manoeuvre safely.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="road"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">06</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 06</span></div><h3>MSM / PSL</h3><p>Use the core observation and manoeuvre routines.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Mirror — Signal — Manoeuvre</li><li>Position — Speed — Look</li><li>Observation before changing direction or position</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Make observation a repeatable routine, not an afterthought.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="road"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">07</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 07</span></div><h3>Moving Off and Stopping</h3><p>Move away and stop with control and observation.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Prepare the vehicle before moving</li><li>Observe surroundings before moving off</li><li>Controlled stopping and safe positioning</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Practise moving off without rushing the clutch, accelerator or observation.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="road"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">08</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 08</span></div><h3>Gear Changing</h3><p>Coordinate speed, clutch and gears smoothly.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Choose a suitable gear for the situation</li><li>Coordinate clutch release and acceleration</li><li>Change gear without losing control</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Aim for smoothness and appropriate gear selection rather than speed.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="road"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">09</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 09</span></div><h3>Uphill, Downhill &amp; Angle Start</h3><p>Manage starts and vehicle control on slopes.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Starting on an uphill or downhill</li><li>Control while approaching a slope</li><li>Awareness of vehicle movement and surrounding traffic</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Use the correct control sequence and avoid rolling.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="road"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">10</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 10</span></div><h3>Emergency Stop</h3><p>Respond safely when an immediate stop is required.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Recognise the need for an emergency stop</li><li>Brake firmly while maintaining control</li><li>Secure the vehicle after stopping</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Emergency stopping should be decisive, controlled and followed by a safety check.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="road"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">11</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 11</span></div><h3>Road Positioning</h3><p>Choose a safe and appropriate position on the road.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Maintain suitable road position</li><li>Consider lane and road layout</li><li>Position early for turns and other manoeuvres</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Good positioning makes your next action predictable and safer.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="road"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">12</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 12</span></div><h3>Major Road → Minor Road: Left</h3><p>Turn left from a major road into a minor road.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Observe the junction and traffic</li><li>Apply MSM / PSL</li><li>Control speed and complete the left turn safely</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Set position and speed before the turn; keep observation active through it.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="road"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">13</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 13</span></div><h3>Major Road → Minor Road: Right</h3><p>Turn right from a major road into a minor road.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Observe traffic and road position</li><li>Apply the correct signal and speed</li><li>Complete the turn with controlled steering</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Right turns require especially careful observation of approaching traffic.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="road"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">14</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 14</span></div><h3>T-Junction: Turning Left</h3><p>Emerging from a T-junction and turning left.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Approach and stop with a clear view</li><li>Observe before emerging</li><li>Turn left with safe positioning</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Do not emerge until the available view and traffic situation are understood.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="road"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">15</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 15</span></div><h3>T-Junction: Turning Right</h3><p>Emerging from a T-junction and turning right.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Position and observation at the junction</li><li>Judge traffic before emerging</li><li>Complete the right turn safely</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Take the time needed for a clear, safe gap.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="traffic"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">16</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 16</span></div><h3>Cross Junction</h3><p>Handle traffic movement through a cross junction.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Observe all relevant approaches</li><li>Use MSM / PSL as appropriate</li><li>Select a safe path through the junction</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Scan the whole junction rather than focusing on only the vehicle directly ahead.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="traffic"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">17</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 17</span></div><h3>Passing Stationary Vehicles</h3><p>Pass parked or stationary vehicles safely.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Observe around the obstruction</li><li>Check for pedestrians and opposing traffic</li><li>Move around the obstruction with control</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Create enough space and be prepared to slow or stop if the view is restricted.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="traffic"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">18</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 18</span></div><h3>Overtaking</h3><p>Understand the controlled sequence for overtaking.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Observation and judgement before overtaking</li><li>Safe position and sufficient visibility</li><li>Return to the lane only when safe</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Overtaking depends on a clear view, adequate space and correct judgement.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="manoeuvres"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">19</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 19</span></div><h3>Reversing Exercise: Straight, Left, Right</h3><p>Build controlled reversing skills in different directions.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Reverse in a straight line</li><li>Reverse with left and right changes</li><li>Continuous observation while reversing</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Keep speed very low and use observation throughout the manoeuvre.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="manoeuvres"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">20</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 20</span></div><h3>Turn in the Road</h3><p>Turn the vehicle around safely within the road.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Understand the available road space</li><li>Use controlled steering and reversing movements</li><li>Observe before each movement</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Break the manoeuvre into deliberate stages and keep checking the surroundings.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="manoeuvres"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">21</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 21</span></div><h3>Vertical Parking</h3><p>Park accurately in a vertical parking space.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Approach and position correctly</li><li>Use reference points and observation</li><li>Finish straight, controlled and safely</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Practise the steering sequence slowly until the entry and final position feel consistent.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="manoeuvres"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">22</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 22</span></div><h3>Angular Parking</h3><p>Enter an angled parking space with control.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Choose the correct approach line</li><li>Steer into the space smoothly</li><li>Check final position and surroundings</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Use observation and a controlled steering arc rather than rushing the entry.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="manoeuvres"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">23</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 23</span></div><h3>Parallel Parking</h3><p>Park safely alongside the kerb or road edge.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Set up the approach</li><li>Use controlled reversing and steering</li><li>Check distance and final position</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Use the reference sequence taught by the instructor and keep checking the surroundings.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="traffic"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">24</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 24</span></div><h3>Roundabout</h3><p>Approach, enter and leave a roundabout safely.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Observe traffic already on the roundabout</li><li>Choose the correct approach and lane</li><li>Signal and exit with control</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Plan your exit before entering and keep observing throughout the roundabout.</div></div></div></article>
      <article class="lesson-card" data-category="traffic"><button class="lesson-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><div class="lesson-top"><span class="lesson-number">25</span><span class="lesson-page">IDTR LESSON 25</span></div><h3>Traffic Signal</h3><p>Understand and respond correctly to traffic signals.</p><span class="lesson-more">Open lesson <b>→</b></span></button><div class="lesson-detail"><div class="lesson-detail-grid"><div><h4>Understand</h4><ul><li>Green, amber and red signals</li><li>Flashing and signal situations shown in the guide</li><li>Stop / proceed decisions at signals</li></ul></div><div class="practice"><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the signal, observe the road and make the correct controlled response.</div></div></div></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="learn-path" id="path">
  <div class="learn-path-inner">
    <div class="learn-path-head"><div><div class="learn-kicker">03 / HOW TO USE THIS HUB</div><h2>Learn. Practise.<br><span>Then drive.</span></h2></div><p>This page is a study companion, not a replacement for supervised practical instruction. Use the concepts here to arrive at your lesson prepared, then practise them with your instructor.</p></div>
    <div class="path-steps">
      <article class="path-step"><b>01</b><h3>Understand</h3><p>Read the lesson and learn the purpose of the skill.</p></article>
      <article class="path-step"><b>02</b><h3>Observe</h3><p>Know what to check before the vehicle moves.</p></article>
      <article class="path-step"><b>03</b><h3>Practise</h3><p>Repeat the skill slowly under supervision.</p></article>
      <article class="path-step"><b>04</b><h3>Combine</h3><p>Use the skill together with observation and control.</p></article>
      <article class="path-step"><b>05</b><h3>Drive right</h3><p>Carry the habit into real road situations.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="learn-cta">
  <div class="learn-cta-inner">
    <div><div class="learn-kicker" style="color:var(--yellow)">READY FOR THE PRACTICAL?</div><h2>Take the lesson<br><span>onto the road.</span></h2><p>Once you understand the basics, the next step is supervised practice. Start your training with Raju Driving School in Chalakudy.</p><a class="btn btn-yellow" href="./index.html#contact">Enquire about training <b>↗</b></a></div>
    <div class="learn-cta-card"><strong>Your basic-learning checklist</strong><ul><li>Know the cockpit drill</li><li>Understand foot, hand and auxiliary controls</li><li>Use MSM / PSL deliberately</li><li>Understand turns, junctions and positioning</li><li>Build reversing and parking control</li><li>Recognise traffic signals and road situations</li></ul></div>
  </div>
</section>
</main>
<script>
const cards=[...document.querySelectorAll('.lesson-card')];
document.querySelectorAll('.lesson-summary').forEach(btn=>btn.addEventListener('click',()=>{const card=btn.closest('.lesson-card');const open=card.classList.toggle('open');btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded',String(open));}));
document.querySelectorAll('[data-filter]').forEach(btn=>btn.addEventListener('click',()=>{document.querySelectorAll('[data-filter]').forEach(b=>b.classList.remove('active'));btn.classList.add('active');const f=btn.dataset.filter;cards.forEach(c=>c.hidden=f!=='all'&&c.dataset.category!==f);document.getElementById('lessons').scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'start'});}));
</script>
</body>
</html>
